#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65a1ba53-d9ca-5ff1-9f3d-9c4fc0989396" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294809} {:answer/id #uuid "dfbe921f-67d0-5706-a5c6-36b025c7070d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294810} {:answer/id #uuid "35cf3d11-b2c5-5e9f-acba-db3eb0fbcd21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294811} {:answer/id #uuid "0c319097-9c82-5855-844a-1c3b6a816381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294812} {:answer/id #uuid "93dc7b26-4f82-599a-a051-8216bdcf5712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93dc7b26-4f82-599a-a051-8216bdcf5712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294813} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b1e9640-f0e5-54fd-a3ed-9808ca7fd7ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "694ae25e-76dc-5254-b28a-52858f45659d" :question/math-academy-id "q-81106" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}}=-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}+\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{10}}=\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}]}
